[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m The real part of the expression is \(324\cos\theta - 444\sin\theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of the sinusoidal function. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 444\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 444^2}\).
