[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m [response] To find the largest possible real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\), we can use the properties of complex numbers and their magnitudes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m Let \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then, we can rewrite the expression in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m And,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta} = (24 - 36i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m = 24\cos\theta - 24i\sin\theta - 36i\cos\theta - 36\sin\theta = 24\cos\theta - 36\sin\theta - i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m Combining these, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + 24\cos\theta - 36\sin\theta - i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta - 36\sin\theta + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) - (24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta - 36\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta - 36\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta) + i(276\sin\theta + 432\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to maximize the expression \(324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta\). The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 504\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 504^2}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 504^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 254016} = \sqrt{359000} = 180\sqrt{11}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m Therefore, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(180\sqrt{11}\). The final answer is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=283795)[0m \boxed{180\sqrt{11}}
